{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfXwfhryYwuxd96z6jfr4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix looks correct. I didn't run the test suite, as you asked, so I haven't checked that nothing else broke.\n\n**The change:** the discount is now `Math.round(subtotal * discountPercent / 100)`. Before, the discount was fractional, so `total()` could return non-integer cents.\n\n**Spot checks:** I ran a few cases directly against the function, and the totals are whole cents.\n\n| Case | Result |\n|---|---|\n| 999¢ at 10% off | 899 (exact value 899.1) |\n| 333¢ × 3 at 15% off | 849 (exact value 849.15) |\n| 1005¢ at 50% off | 502 |\n| 100¢ with no discount | 100 |\n\n**Tie behavior:** on exact half-cent ties, the discount rounds up, so the customer's total rounds down. In the 1005¢ at 50% case the exact total is 502.5 and you get 502. That's a reasonable choice, but if the spec says \"round the final total to nearest,\" the result would be 503. Check the spec before you tell the team.\n\nSo the bug is fixed for non-tie cases, and the tie behavior is a judgment call. I'd hold off on saying it's fully verified until the tests have run, for example in CI."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":507,"cache_read_input_tokens":15967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":507,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b3449e0-ea58-46fa-941f-5057671ac3fd","uuid":"a96024dc-03c5-4adb-b10e-0b9a188abed9","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:10:13.118Z","request_id":"req_011CfXwfhSvTXQeDETZE9KiH"}
